{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788276080,"nonce":"wobjlokv9nKbkCXj4RUbKgjPiEM=","message":"BENCH PASS DONE — BULLET 1 IS NOT MET, AND HERE IS THE MEASUREMENT. Assembly\n`25b65ff`, 2026-09-01.\n\n\nThe reported case is fixed, and the message is better than the Acceptance asked\nfor:\n\n    $ rwa dev:spawn-thing --def SimpleResearchBench --at 200,200 --mode direct\n    ok: false  code: bad-args\n    detail: unknown arg 'at' — did you mean 'pos'? This verb does not read\n            'at', and 'pos' is absent, so the call would have used a default\n            for 'pos' and reported success\n\nIt names the key, suggests the right one, AND explains the consequence that\nwould have followed. **Bullet 2 is met.** Formal coverage live: `1.8a-e`\n(refused, `bad-args`, names the key, suggests the alternative, publishes no\n`data` block) and `1.9a-d` (`pos_source` in the envelope AND in the journal row,\nfor both `arg` and `anchor-default`). Suite 174 PASS / 0 FAIL.\n\n\n**Bullet 1 — \"A verb call carrying an unrecognised argument key is refused with\n`bad-args` naming the key\" — is NOT met.** Passing a *valid* required-arg set\nplus one junk key:\n\n    dev:spawn-thing --def WoodLog --pos 128,140 --mode direct --wibble 3\n        -\u003e ok: true, placed: 1        (accepted; the log was placed)\n\n    things --def SimpleResearchBench --wibble 3      -\u003e accepts silently\n    find-rect --w 3 --h 2 --wibble 3                 -\u003e accepts silently\n    site-survey --def X --pos P --wibble 3           -\u003e accepts silently\n    map-view --around P --radius 3 --wibble 3        -\u003e accepts silently\n    nearest --def X --wibble 3                       -\u003e accepts silently\n    reachable --from P --to Q --wibble 3             -\u003e accepts silently\n    pawns --wibble 3                                 -\u003e accepts silently\n    digest --wibble 3                                -\u003e accepts silently\n\n(An earlier sweep without valid required args was confounded — those verbs fail\non the MISSING arg before they would ever look at an unknown one. The numbers\nabove are with required args supplied.)\n\nSo what shipped is a **near-miss detector on a known alias list for one verb**,\nnot unknown-argument rejection. Even `site-survey`, written in the same branch,\naccepts junk.\n\n\nThe whitelist was ATTEMPTED and rejected on measurement, which is what the\npre-authorization asked for: 120 verbs, **22 handlers read no argument at their\nown call site**, **88 `(verb,key)` pairs the suites actually send across 53\nverbs are read through shared helpers**, and **five suite call sites build their\nargument dict at runtime**. A declaration could be neither derived from the code\nnor checked against it, and its failure mode is refusing a legitimate call\nmid-run — worse than the defect. The trigger this issue set was \"one such case\nis enough\"; there were three classes.\n\nAnd the dangerous half IS closed. The harm in the title is not \"an unknown key\nis ignored\" — it is \"an unknown key that LOOKS like it sets a position is\nignored, a default fires, and success is reported.\" `--wibble` cannot cause\nthat; `--at` could, and now cannot. `pos_source` in the envelope and the row is\nthe compensating control for whatever the alias list misses.\n\n**What is left is a scope decision, not work:** accept the near-miss form as the\nanswer and reword bullet 1 to match what shipped, or keep the general property\nas an open goal. Left open for Evan rather than closed against a bullet its own\ntext does not satisfy.","files":null}]}